{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://aureline.dev/schemas/ai/m5-draft-state-row-attachment-stale-banner-and-send-review-control.schema.json",
  "title": "Aureline M5 draft-state-row / attachment-stale-banner / send-review-control primitive",
  "description": "Export-safe packet implementing the reusable M5 draft-state row, the offline-local-only / attachment-stale banner, and the split-send-or-review control as one primitive trio. The packet binds one row per claimed send-capable composer consumer — the inline composer, the side panel, the patch draft, the CLI / headless surface, and the support export — to the shared draft, stale-banner, and send-control anatomy, the derived retention posture (local_only_ephemeral/local_only_persisted/workspace_retained/account_retained/shared_to_thread/purge_pending), the derived banner posture (fresh/offline_local_only/stale_refreshable/stale_superseded_review/stale_source_gone/stale_access_revoked), the derived send posture (ready_to_send/split_send_review/review_before_send/policy_blocked/over_budget_blocked/taint_blocked), the bounded qualified send paths (explain_only/review_then_send/direct_send), the draft / banner / send bounded actions, export fields, and non-visual accessibility routes. A self-describing vocabulary set freezes the controlled vocabulary. Each row carries worked draft, banner, and send resolution cases proving the resolvers, and four hard invariants: it never masks draft locality or retention, never assumes hidden sharing, never invents a private send grammar, and never collapses a high-authority send into one unqualified affordance. Raw prompts, draft bodies, attachment bodies, raw paths, raw URLs, credentials, and private endpoints never cross this boundary.",
